==English==
{{was wotd|2012|July|24}}
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|sagacité|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|sagācitās|lang=la||sagaciousness}}, from {{term|sagāx|lang=la||of quick perception, acute, sagacious}}, from {{term|sāgiō|lang=la||I perceive by the senses}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/səˈɡæsəti/|/səˈɡæsɪti/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|sagacities}}

# The quality of being [[sage]], [[wise]], or able to make good decisions.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|wisdom}}
* {{l|en|sagaciousness}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|sagacious}}

